              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_sql_fund_alias_distinct.s05.b01",
              "role": "definition",
              "text": "SELECT DISTINCT removes duplicate rows from the result, keeping one row from each group of duplicates. SELECT DISTINCT city FROM customers returns each city exactly once, no matter how many customers share it. SELECT ALL — the default when DISTINCT is not written — keeps every row, duplicates included.",
              "lineage": {
