              "role": "takeaway",
              "text": "A table alias — FROM orders AS o — is a temporary rename that exists only for the current query. Once assigned, use the alias, not the original name. Column aliases work the same way in the SELECT list. SELECT DISTINCT collapses duplicate rows so each unique value appears once; without it, SELECT ALL is the default and every row is kept.",
